--------------------------------------------------


5. DEPOT MANAGER APPROVAL

Depot Managers must approve:

- Collector information.
- Plastic transaction details.
- Weight records.
- Verification photographs.

Business Rule:

No payout may occur without manager approval.



--------------------------------------------------


6. PAYMENT PROCESSING WORKFLOW

After approval:

- Transaction is locked.
- Database row is locked.
- Payment payload is generated.
- Telecom API request is sent.
- Telecom response is recorded.

Business Rule:

Transactions cannot be processed twice.



--------------------------------------------------


7. PAYMENT FAILURE HANDLING

Possible failure scenarios:

- Network timeout.
- Telecom rejection.
- Invalid account.
- Collector wallet limitations.
- API communication failures.

Failed transactions are permanently logged.



--------------------------------------------------


8. STUCK PENDING PROTOCOL

If the telecom provider does not return a confirmed response:

- Transaction becomes STUCK_PENDING.
- No automatic payout retry occurs.
- Transaction remains locked.

Business Rule:

The system must never risk duplicate payouts.



--------------------------------------------------


9. PAYMENT RETRY PROTOCOL

A secure reconciliation process runs every fifteen minutes.

The system:

- Checks telecom transaction status.
- Verifies payment execution.
- Unlocks transactions only when confirmed safe.

Business Rule:

Only verified failed transactions may be retried.



--------------------------------------------------


10. OFFLINE PAYMENT PROTOCOL

If payment services are unavailable:

- Transaction status becomes APPROVED_OFFLINE.
- Collector receives a secure payout voucher.
- Payment is processed once network services are restored.



--------------------------------------------------


11. CORPORATE WALLET PROTECTION RULES

Payments are blocked if:

- Float balance is insufficient.
- Collector limits are exceeded.
- Depot limits are exceeded.
- Telecom validation fails.
- Manager approval is missing.



--------------------------------------------------


12. TRANSACTION LIMITS

Transaction Limits:

- Maximum Single Transaction: 50,000 CFA.

Daily Collector Limit:

- Maximum: 150,500 CFA.

Daily Depot Limit:

- Maximum: 500,000 CFA.

Business Rule:

Only the WastePay Super Administrator may override financial limits.



--------------------------------------------------


13. FLOAT THRESHOLD ALERTS

If corporate float balances drop below:

- 200,000 CFA

The system immediately notifies the WastePay Super Administrator.



--------------------------------------------------


14. MOBILE MONEY RECEIPTS

Successful payouts generate:

- SMS receipt.
- Digital transaction receipt.
- Telecom reference number.

Receipts include:

- Transaction ID.
- Amount paid.
- Total kilograms.
- Payment provider.
- Payment timestamp.



--------------------------------------------------


15. MOBILE MONEY TRANSACTION RECORDS

The system permanently stores:

- Transaction ID.
- Collector ID.
- Collector phone number.
- Telecom provider.
- Provider reference number.
- Amount paid.
- Depot ID.
- Payment status.
- Approval timestamps.
- Telecom response records.



--------------------------------------------------


16. FINANCIAL AUDIT TRAIL

Financial records are immutable.

The following actions are prohibited:

- Delete.
- Edit.
- Overwrite.

Corrections require:

ADJUSTMENT TRANSACTIONS ONLY.



--------------------------------------------------


17. END OF DAY RECONCILIATION

Every evening the system automatically compares:

- Total kilograms collected.
- Total payments disbursed.
- Depot transaction totals.
- Mobile Money payout totals.

Any variance is flagged for administrative review.



--------------------------------------------------


18. COLLECTOR PAYMENT HISTORY

Collectors may view:

- Total earnings.
- Daily earnings.
- Weekly earnings.
- Monthly earnings.
- Payment history.
- Digital receipts.
- Total kilograms collected.



--------------------------------------------------


19. BUSINESS RULES

- Every payout requires account validation.
- Every payout requires manager approval.
- Transactions are immutable.
- Duplicate payouts are prohibited.
- Payments are blocked when limits are exceeded.
- Payment retries are strictly controlled.
- Financial records are permanently stored.


